    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d41">

                <pb facs="0172" n="73" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg73"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.60d31/136½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Mr. Landreth M. Harrison of the Division
                        of Eastern European Affairs</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-01-17">January 17, 1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The original and three copies of the attached United States reply<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d41-f1"/> to Finnish counter-proposals for the general
                        provisions<anchor n="3" xml:id="d41-f2"/> to be included in the proposed
                    American-Finnish trade agreement were delivered to the Finnish Minister<anchor
                        n="4" xml:id="d41-f3"/> today, together with the original and three copies
                    of the attached comments thereon.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d41-f4"/> This reply will
                    be studied in the Finnish Legation over the week-end and the Minister or Dr. von
                        Numers<anchor n="5" xml:id="d41-f5"/> will call at the Department in the
                    event that any further information with respect thereto is desired before the
                    full text is referred to the Finnish Foreign Office.</p>
                <closer><signed>L. M. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
